abstract: >-
  ThoxOS is the operating system for THOX's local-first AI devices
  and desktops. Its record has two foundations in four days: the
  v0.1.0 whitepaper of 31 October specified linux-thox, a Linux LTS
  fork with a separate Rust research laboratory; the 0.2.0-review
  draft of 1 November identifies ThoxInux, a Ginux-derived Rust-first
  x86-64 kernel with Linux userspace compatibility, as the reviewed
  foundation, and treats the whitepaper as historical input. This
  report takes the reviewed foundation as the architecture of record,
  keeps what the whitepaper specified that survives the change (class
  floors, entitlement without DRM, A/B updates with a health gate,
  the open and paid line), and adds the evidence a general host can
  produce.
keywords:
